<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    The placeholder generator (M8-10): one recognisably-fake, id-stamped image per runtime art slot
    in M8-09's register, driven through M8-06's `15` §B4 seven-step pipeline and graded by Part F.

    Why it exists: six of M8's eight original tasks are ⛔ capability-blocked (no agent can run
    Midjourney), so the real art does not exist and will not until a human session generates it.
    Everything downstream of art — screens, atlases, the QA gate itself — is blocked on *something*
    being in every slot. These placeholders are that something, and every one of them is scaffolding
    a real asset overwrites. This project authors no art.

    🔒 OUTPUT GOES TO artifacts/ (gitignored). NEVER assets/. M8-01a's delivery scan walks the
    FILESYSTEM, not the git index, and demands a provenance record for every .png under assets/. An
    uncommitted placeholder run under assets/ would redden the provenance gate for every developer
    on the repository. Nothing this tool writes is ever committed.

    🔒 RULING A8 (M8, 2026-08-12): nothing is written under game-data/. LocalFileContentSource
    enumerates every *.json there into the ContentSnapshot whose hash `14` §6 makes load-bearing for
    replay and CONTENT_VERSION_MISMATCH.

    🔒 It reuses all three merged dependencies and builds no fourth of anything (steering S12):
    SlayIdleRepeat.AssetManifest is the only manifest reader, SlayIdleRepeat.AssetPipeline is the
    only implementation of `15` §B4 and Part F, and SlayIdleRepeat.AssetProvenance is the only
    provenance record format. There is no second naming implementation and no parallel QA path here.

    🔒 SkiaSharp is NOT PackageReference'd. It arrives transitively through the ProjectReference to
    tools/AssetPipeline, which keeps ProjectFileTests.Vendor_package_is_referenced_by_exactly_one_project
    both green AND armed: that rule reads PackageReference Include attributes out of production
    .csproj files, so naming SkiaSharp here would fire it and would spread a native-binary dependency
    to a second project for no gain.

    🔒 No native binaries. Nothing shells out to ImageMagick, pngquant, oxipng or a font rasteriser.
    The id stamp is drawn from a 5×7 bitmap font declared in this project (StampFont), not from an
    SKTypeface: a system font is not guaranteed to exist on CI's ubuntu-24.04 runner and would make
    the output differ between machines.

    Its architecture category is ToolProjectAccountabilityTests.PipelineConsumerToolNames — see the
    rule stated there for what it may and may not reference.
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <RootNamespace>SlayIdleRepeat.AssetPlaceholders</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>SlayIdleRepeat.AssetPlaceholders</AssemblyName>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <InvariantGlobalization>true</InvariantGlobalization>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\AssetManifest\SlayIdleRepeat.AssetManifest.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\AssetPipeline\SlayIdleRepeat.AssetPipeline.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\AssetProvenance\SlayIdleRepeat.AssetProvenance.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
